meta {
  name: 78 Inventory Settings
  seq: 78
}

docs {
  # Inventory Settings

  Business Admin › Business Settings › Inventory Settings — tenant-level toggles
  that control how inventory is deducted for orders. Tenant-scoped (RLS),
  tenant-level: the tenant comes from the JWT, never a body field. Stored in the
  tenant's `business_inventory_settings` row (NOT the inventory app's
  `inventory_settings`; the two apps share this database).

  Two settings:
  - `isAutomaticInventoryReductionEnabled` (boolean, default `false`) — when ON,
    inventory is auto-deducted at order creation via the existing proforma
    consumption flow; when OFF, no automatic deduction happens and stock is managed
    manually from Technician Reporting.
  - `manualAdjustmentMode` (`ORDER_TYPE` | `TEST_TYPE`, default `ORDER_TYPE`) —
    where manual inventory adjustment is offered: once per order, or once per test.

  Permissions (module `business_admin`, section "Inventory Settings"):
  - read is ungated for any authenticated business user (the Technician Reporting
    page reads `manualAdjustmentMode` to decide which adjustment action to show).
  - `business_admin:inventory_settings__update_inventory_settings` — save (a
    Business Admin holds it by default; the role also bypasses the guard).

  Use a Business Admin token (`{{businessAccessToken}}`).
}
